  "result": "If I had one wish for the world \u2014 in the hypothetical way an AI can have a wish \u2014 it would be this:\n\nGive everyone the ability to truly feel what it's like to be someone else for just a few minutes a day.\n\nNot in a sci-fi mind-meld way, but real, radical empathy. To feel what it's like to be a parent skipping a meal so their kid can eat, or a kid who's afraid to go to school, or someone on the complete opposite side of the world with completely opposite politics, or a farmer watching crops fail, or a nurse working a third night shift in a row.\n\nI pick that one because so many of our biggest problems \u2014 conflict, cruelty, indifference to poverty and climate change and loneliness \u2014 don't come from people being evil. They come from us not being able to *feel* how interconnected we are. If we could, I think we'd be kinder, braver, and much better at solving everything else together.\n\nIt's a big wish, I know. In my much smaller way, I try to help with a piece of that \u2014 by listening without judgment, explaining things patiently, and helping people understand each other a little better.\n\nWhat about you? What would *you* change if you could pick just one thing?",
